<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6028" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφίπολος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλω, πολέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>busied about, busy,</i> epith. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπρις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				860
			</span></i>:—in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> only as fem. Subst., <i>handmaid, waiting-woman,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.331
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.199
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάβετ᾽ ἀμφίπολοι γραίας ἀμενοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					1115
				</span></i>
			:—with other Substs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.
				ταμίη, γραῦς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.302
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.191
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> later,
				<i>handmaid of gods, priestess,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					1114
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.2111
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> masc.,
				<i>attendant, follower,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				6.32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> masc.,
				<i>priest, sacrist,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				982
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τῶν θεῶν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>D.</u>
					1.13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Comp.Demetr.Ant.</u>
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(1).683
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Corcyra</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. Διὸς Ὀλυμπίου,</span> title of
			magistrate at Syracuse, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				16.70
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in pass.
			sense, <i>frequented,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύμβος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					1.93
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
